e should remove all meditation outside of a 'temple' butmaybe we could reduce the healing rate outside of that player's guild rooms.Seems to me that being in their temple, or at their shrine, or whatever,should heal them faster, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: haploFwd:  healingCc: archesDate: Nov  1To: airborneRe:   healingCc: archesDate: Oct 31I don't know that we should remove all meditation outside of a 'temple' butmaybe we could reduce the healing rate outside of that player's guild rooms.Seems to me that being in their temple, or at their shrine, or whatever,should heal them faster, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: haploSubj: healing...Cc: archesDate: Nov  1Sorry about that, zigged when I should have zagged.Here's the idea that I have been bouncing about in my head.  Ok, suppose we limit meditation/healing skills to only the guild roomand \"shrines\".  Then we give guild members the ability to create shrines in various locations.  Players will be able to have their healing, but they would have to work a bit for it.  To start, we'd have the shrine needed to be built.  An easy way toget players to spend a bunch of gold on all sorts of things, bowls, statues, insense, etc.  Then they would have to protect those locationsonce they were built.  Certainly leaving lots of valuables laying around would tempt almost any player, which would kinda be the point.Add in the idea that some elements of theshrine would degrade withtime (insence comes to mind) and have to be replaced every so often.  The idea is to create an economy by finding reasons for players to gatheror purchase things that aren't just for killing.  If insence were onlyavailable in a small handful of locations, and there was a demand for itwe'd create the demand.  It helps control healing rates, keeps moneydown a bit, adds a roleplaying element to the mud, and encourages guildsto work together.Ideas and critics?**mangla**To: exosSubj: AttitudeCc: archesDate: Nov 16If you have a problem with people then take it upwith them in private. This continued harangueing ofothers on the public boards is getting out of hand.Sit back, take a deep breath and lets get on with moresensible things.-Mangla**mangla**To: tatsuoSubj: ezo coastCc: archesDate: Mar  9I had to fix up players/tatsuo/ezo/coast/genCoast.cthis morning. This is the second day in a row thatareas of Ezo would not load. Please be more careful whenchanging things. All errors are simple. Missing ;or extra \" and in this case one of the problems wasa function redefinition.-Mangla**mangla**To: tatsuoSubj: arenaCc: exos, archesDate: Mar 19I had another though. If we get enough people. I would notmind seeing two arena a day when it makes sense. But thesecond arena would be open for lower levels. So be carefulwhen opening the arenas, and if there are more lower levelson then exclude the higher levels, or have two.the syntax, in case you had/have problems is:open arena <min>-<max>-Mangla**mangla**To: thumperSubj: ExosCc: archesDate: Mar 22I have a set of complaints, and we are watching to catchhim in the act. So far the only act was have caught him inis talking to kitty. Nothing threatening. If he is guilty,then he will slip up. At that time, caught red-handed,we will do it. Have some patience. It will be addressed.As for Tatsuo. That will be taken care of in its owntime also. There are many many facts that have beenleft out. There are no insecurity issues.-Manglaarches**mangla**To: sargonSubj: PromotionsCc: arches, tinman, shadowmonk, brainsprain, redsexy, bobo, turboDate: Mar 31As was promised, the promotions have been made.Thanks for your time and patience.-Mangla**brainsprain**To: turboSubj: bard skillCc: archesDate: Apr  8     One of the bard skills somehow allows a bard to sidestep a backstab.This does not make snese to me, how can you sidestep an attack thatyou do not know is coming, it is not even like the bard guild is a guild who is incredibly dextrious.  If there is a valid skill reason for this, Iwould like to know, otherwise it should be changed, thieves are meantto rely on this one skill, backstab, for most of their damage and it isa onetime only attack, if it is going to be blocked by your guildI need to decide what that means towards my guilds skillsBrainsprain**turbo**To: brainsprainRe:   bard skillCc: archesDate: Apr  8skill?  I can think of a spell, irish luck, but a skill?Irish luck has a LONG recast time, and from my understanding of itgives AT BEST 15 dodges.  While this may seem like a lot,keep in mind that the shadow lasts longer than 9000 seconds, which is the MAX time for their Armour of ithan.Also, how did this come to be known?Why was a thief backstabbing a bard to begin with.Oh, and as far as not know its comming, that is why its calledIrish Luck.  Luck can account for a lot of things, including avoiding an attack you do not see coming.  While the message this dodgereturns may not be descriptive of the attack,that does not disqualify it.After all, as a player, I have pounded skeletons into a pile of bloodand body parts many times.The message may be innaccurate, but the effect is the same.**brainsprain**To: turboSubj: in reply to bothCc: archesDate: Apr  8Yeah, arches will mail all of the arches, i think wizzes works as wellto send to everybody.As to to skill or spell, that is fine, what happened was malice and treatwere in the arena and I was watching the battle over malices shoulder.I watched treat sidestep a backstab, which made no sense whatsoever to me.  When i asked him how he did ithe refused to cooperate, so i asked him if it was a skill, an